toring of coagulation parameters when starting or discontinuing 甲氰脒胍. This effect appears independent of H₂-receptor blockade, as structurally distinct H₂ antagonists like ranitidine do not produce similar metabolic interference [Data: Relationships (3340)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"甲氰脒胍 is contraindicated in patients with liver disease\",\n            \"explanation\": \"甲氰脒胍 is contraindicated for use in 肝脏病人 (patients with liver disease). This precaution arises from its impact on hepatic metabolism: 甲氰脒胍 reduces liver blood flow and inhibits microsomal enzyme activity, which can exacerbate drug accumulation and toxicity in individuals with compromised liver function. Given that many drugs metabolized by the liver are already at higher risk of toxicity in this population, adding 甲氰脒胍 further increases the likelihood of adverse events, including fatal complications. Therefore, alternative therapies should be considered for liver-impaired patients requiring gastric acid suppression [Data: Entities (14929); Relationships (6813)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"甲氰脒胍’s mechanism involves dual pathways: hepatic enzyme inhibition and renal effects\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The drug interaction profile of 甲氰脒胍 stems from two primary mechanisms: inhibition of hepatic microsomal enzymes (especially cytochrome P-450) and potential impairment of renal excretion. While its hepatic effects are well-documented—leading to reduced clearance of high-extraction drugs like phenytoin and benzodiazepines—甲氰脒胍 has also been reported to cause interstitial nephritis, resulting in renal dysfunction. This secondary effect can elevate serum concentrations of renally excreted drugs. Together, these mechanisms explain the wide range of clinically relevant interactions observed with 甲氰脒胍 across diverse drug classes [Data: Relationships (3346, 3342, 3340)].\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 7.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The comm